The variable `n1` returns the value 20.0, which is the result of computing the base-2 logarithm of 1048576.0 (since 2^20 equals 1048576). The variable `n2` returns the value 0.0, representing the result of adding the computed base-2 logarithm of 0.001 to the negative of the epsilon constant (approximately -9.965784284662087), effectively canceling out the small logarithmic value to produce zero within floating-point precision.

