The call `nth 1 i0` returns the number of free KiB in the boot arena, while `nth 1 i1` returns the remaining free KiB after 100 workers have completed their tasks. The call `nth 2 i1` retrieves the count of memory requests queued on the actor, and `nth 3 i1` retrieves the count of requests currently parked (waiting) on the actor. These values are used to calculate `pct`, which represents the percentage of memory remaining free relative to the initial free amount, allowing the test to verify that the memory manager successfully served requests without running out of space.

```sol
