To calculate the recoil position, use the `recoil` function with the attacker's identifier `s`, the current time `t`, and the current position `(x, y, zz)`. The function determines a recoil distance based on whether the time is less than 60 milliseconds; if so, the distance is zero, otherwise it applies an eased-out curve scaled by 90 units and the direction of the attacker. The result is the original position minus the scaled direction vector.

```sol
recoil s t (x, y, zz) =
  k = case t < 60 of True -> 0 | False -> easeOut (clampK ((300 - t) * 1000 / 240)) * 90 / 1000;
  (x, y, zz - dirOf s * k);
```

