The `epoch` function implements a single iteration of the training loop for a polynomial regression model by calculating gradients and updating weights using the stochastic gradient descent algorithm. It takes the current number of iterations, learning rate, and polynomial coefficients as inputs, then processes a vector of data points to compute the sum of squared residuals and their partial derivatives with respect to each coefficient. Specifically, it uses `Vec.fold` to accumulate these gradient values across the dataset, normalizes them by the dataset size `n`, and returns the updated coefficients and the final vector of data points.

```sol
epoch n lr a b c v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (gA a b c) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (gB a b c) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (gC a b c) 0 v2;
  (a - lr * (s1 / n), b - lr * (s2 / n), c - lr * (s3 / n), v3).
```

