The `advance` function processes a single event within the QOS operating system to update the system state, ensuring a consistent view of changes across all participants. It first journals the event if the configuration requires it, then applies the event to the model to generate commands. Next, it persists the updated model to the database and executes the generated commands. Finally, it broadcasts the new version number to all active sessions, settles the state if the event caused a quit, or returns the updated state for the next tick.

```fprisc
advance me ev st = case st of
  Rs cfg app model sessions nextSid db saved tickers version told ->
    _ = (if cfg.journal then journal app.codec db ev else Unit);
    (case app.update ev model of (model2, cmds) ->
         saved2 = persist me app.fields db model2 saved;
         quit = perform me sessions cmds;
         told2 = broadcast me (M.values sessions) (version + 1) told;
         (if quit then _ = settle app.fields db model2 saved2; _ = goodbye (M.values sessions); O.None
          else O.Some (startTickers me (Rs cfg app model2 sessions nextSid db saved2 tickers (version + 1) told2)))).
```

The `advance` function first journals the event if the configuration requires it, then updates the model and persists changes. If the update commands result in a quit state, the function settles the model and sends a stop signal to all active sessions via `goodbye`; otherwise, it starts new tickers with an incremented version number to broadcast state changes to all writers.

```fprisc
advance me ev st = case st of Rs cfg app model sessions nextSid db saved tickers version told ->
