The `clockStr` function formats the system time by first retrieving the current clock ticks via `svcClock`, converting them to seconds (assuming a 10 MHz virtual clock rate), and then calculating minutes and seconds. It relies on the `pad2` helper to ensure two-digit formatting and `showInt` to convert integers to decimal strings, ultimately concatenating these parts with colons.

```sol
clockStr : unsafe Caps -> String .
clockStr caps =
  s = secsOf (svcClock caps);
  mm = s / 60;
  ss = s - mm * 60;
  strcat (strcat (pad2 mm) ":") (pad2 ss).
```

