The Sol interpreter was left quadratic while four acceleration tiers were grown on top of it, which is described as the clearest ethos violation in the project tree. This contradicts the project's core principle of simple, elegant code over premature optimization. A typical Sol loop demonstrating quadratic behavior looks like this:
```sol
func count(n) {
  let total = 0;
  for i in range(0, n) {
    total += i;
  }
  return total;
}
```

This was an ethos violation where the core interpreter was intentionally left quadratic to allow four acceleration tiers to grow on top, prioritizing the incremental addition of optimization layers over a linear, optimized baseline. The interpreter's quadratic nature is evident in the Sol pipeline where transactions are processed without immediate linear acceleration:
```sol
(txn : Transaction) -> (txn : Transaction) {
    for i in 0..txn.len {
        for j in 0..i {
            txn.merge(txn[i], txn[j]);
        }
    }
    return txn;
}
```

