The `load` function retrieves data from the store by first converting the query string to lowercase, then deciding whether to call `Store.page` for an empty query or `Store.search` for a non-empty one to fetch rows and a count. It calculates the total number of pages required based on the count and page size, and if the requested page index exceeds the total pages, it automatically loads the last available page to prevent rendering empty results.

```fprisc
load store v =
  q = String.toLower v.q;
  (rows, n) = (if strlen q == 0 then Store.page (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store
               else Store.search (matches q) (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store);
  pages = (if n == 0 then 1 else (n + pageSize - 1) / pageSize);
  (if v.page >= pages and v.page > 0 then load store {v | page = pages - 1}
   else {rows = rows, count = n, total = (if strlen q == 0 then n else Store.count store), pages = pages, page = v.page}).
```

