The `awaitResult` function returns an `Err` value containing the string "poller stopped". This occurs in two scenarios: first, if `A.sendSure` fails to send the watch to the poller, triggering the `else Err "poller stopped"` branch; second, if the subsequent `receiveFrom` operation fails or receives a message other than `Readable`, also resulting in `Err "poller stopped"`.

```sol
awaitResult fd p = case p of Poller a ->
  me = myself 0;
  if A.sendSure me a (Watch fd me) then
    m = receiveFrom me a;
    result = case m of Readable _ -> Ok Unit | _ -> Err "poller stopped";
    _ = drop m;
    result
  else Err "poller stopped".
```

