The `evalStr` function extracts a heap cell, parses its encoded format (requiring a specific range for the string index and a fixed offset), and delegates to `evalBin` if the conditions are met. If the format is invalid, it returns a failure state.

```sol
evalStr f m =
  (m1, tf, fv) = cellAt f m;
  s = fv / 1024;
  ar = fv % 1024;
  case and (and (s >= 2) (s <= 6)) (ar == 2) of
    False -> (m1, Nope)
  | True -> evalBin s f m1.
```

The `evalStr` function evaluates a heap term representing a string by extracting its cell metadata to determine if it contains a valid binary literal. It retrieves the term type and value, calculates the string length (`s`) and offset (`ar`), and checks if the length falls within the range of 2 to 6 and the offset is exactly 2. If these conditions are met, it proceeds to `evalBin`; otherwise, it returns `Nope`.

```sol
evalStr f m =
  (m1, tf, fv) = cellAt f m;
  s = fv / 1024;
  ar = fv % 1024;
  case and (and (s >= 2) (s <= 6)) (ar == 2) of
    False -> (m1, Nope)
  | True -> evalBin s f m1.
```

The `evalStr` function returns a `Got` value containing the string data if the extracted index `s` is between 2 and 6 (inclusive) and the argument index `ar` is exactly 2. In this specific case, it returns `(m1, Got v)` where `m1` is the modified heap and `v` is the string value, as it proceeds to call `evalBin`.

```sol
evalStr f m =
  (m1, tf, fv) = cellAt f m;
  s = fv / 1024;
  ar = fv % 1024;
  case and (and (s >= 2) (s <= 6)) (ar == 2) of
    False -> (m1, Nope)
  | True -> evalBin s f m1.
```

The `evalStr` function first retrieves the heap term's cell content using `cellAt`, then extracts the string value `fv`. It calculates the string length `s` by dividing `fv` by 1024 and the offset `ar` by taking `fv` modulo 1024. The function validates the term only if the string length `s` is between 2 and 6 (inclusive) AND the offset `ar` equals 2; otherwise, it returns `Nope`. If valid, it proceeds to evaluate the binary operation using `evalBin`.

```sol
evalStr f m =
  (m1, tf, fv) = cellAt f m;
  s = fv / 1024;
  ar = fv % 1024;
  case and (and (s >= 2) (s <= 6)) (ar == 2) of
    False -> (m1, Nope)
  | True -> evalBin s f m1.
```

