A QAR2 archive consists of a text header containing a MANIFEST and a LOAD section, followed by a binary IMAGE payload. The LOAD section specifies the absolute base address, the entry point offset relative to that base, the sizes of executable and writable regions, and the total memory span. To load this image, a loader reads the LOAD section to determine the base address, copies the IMAGE payload to that location, and executes at the specified entry offset.

```sol
// Example of parsing the LOAD section from a QAR2 archive
let base = parse_dec("base", load_section);
let entry = parse_dec("entry", load_section);
let execsz = parse_dec("execsz", load_section);
let rwoff = parse_dec("rwoff", load_section);
let imagesz = parse_dec("imagesz", load_section);
let memsz = parse_dec("memsz", load_section);

// Allocate memory at the base address
let mem = alloc(base, memsz);

// Copy the IMAGE payload to the allocated memory
let img = read_payload("IMAGE");
memcpy(mem, img, imagesz);

// Fill the rest of the span with zeros
memset(mem + imagesz, 0, memsz - imagesz);

// Jump to the entry point relative to the base
jmp(base + entry);
```

