The `shell = ...` stamp is a load signature derived from the current shell image's LOAD hash, stamped onto every plugin by `mkqa` to ensure the packaged module matches the exact environment it was compiled against. When `LR.load` attempts to attach a module, the host daemon verifies this stamp against the hosted image; if they do not match, the attach is refused as a named error, preventing silent memory corruption. This mechanism ensures the running module set remains a pure function of the log, as refused versions are detached and never recorded.

