The `step` function processes a single event within the term handler's state machine to update the application model, execute queued commands, manage subscriptions, and render the output. It begins by calling `app.update` to generate a new model and a list of commands. It then executes these commands via `perform`, which may spawn asynchronous tasks for delays or work units. Following command execution, it initializes new subscriptions using `startSubs` and retrieves the visual representation of the model by calling `app.view`. Finally, it paints the screen with the generated lines and returns a new state (or `O.None` if a quit command was issued).

```fprisc
step me app ev st = case st of St model screen cols rows pending ->
  (case app.update ev model of (model2, cmds) ->
      quit = perform me cmds;
      _ = startSubs me (app.subs model2) (app.subs model);
