The HAL (Hardware Abstraction Layer) table is a fixed-width C ABI data structure containing a single pointer to in-memory C functions, designed to test hardware mapping and provide the application with essential runtime operations. It is constructed during stage 1 of the initializer by verifying that the fixed arena can be mapped at the linked address via `mmap MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE`, after which the function pointers are assembled into a `qos_hal_t` object. The application receives this pointer as part of its boot record and uses it to invoke specific C ABI functions directly, bypassing the need for a separate FPRISC runtime to interpret results, which instead return as rendered strings.

