  granted = append (keepGranted (manReq m) reqG) (keepGranted opt optG);
  caps = mkCaps con (ioMe io) (ioClk io) granted (manId m) (ioSt io);
  runEntry con qa m caps.
```

The `launchGranted` function is called to execute an application manifest after both required and optional permissions have been verified and persisted. It requires an unsafe IO4 handle, the application ID string, the manifest object, the string of granted required permissions, and a list of booleans indicating the status of optional permissions.

```sol
launchGranted io qa m stored reqG =
  con = ioCon io;
  opt = manOpt m;
  _ = case opt of Nil -> Unit | _ :: _ -> putLn con "Optional permissions:";
  optG = askAllRem io stored False opt;
  _ = persistPerms io (manId m) stored (manReq m) reqG opt optG;
  granted = append (keepGranted (manReq m) reqG) (keepGranted opt optG);
