The `logActor` function defines the stateless facade for the `/logs` service, handling three primary query types: `LogAdd` to record entries, `LogSnap` to retrieve the current state, and `Read` to fetch a specific log path. It delegates internal operations to the QOS system (`Sys.logAt`, `Sys.logSnap`) and manages state transitions via `logActor` recursion.

```fprisc
logActor me =
  m = receive me;
  (replyTo, q) = m;
  logMsg me replyTo q;

logMsg me replyTo q = case q of
    LogAdd sev line -> logDo me replyTo sev line
  | LogSnap sev -> send replyTo (Sys.logSnap sev) >> logActor me
  | Read path -> send replyTo (joinNl (Sys.logSnap (sevOfPath path))) >> logActor me
  | _ -> error "qsys log: unexpected message";

logDo me replyTo sev line =
  _ = Sys.logAt sev line;
  send replyTo 0 >> logActor me;
```

