The `leadSlack` function calculates the amount of horizontal or vertical space available for a leading child in a layout container when no children are explicitly set to grow. It first determines the total width or height of the children plus their gaps, then subtracts this from the container's available space (accounting for padding). If any children are configured to grow, the function returns zero; otherwise, it returns half of the remaining space, using integer division.

```fpr
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

