The `compact` function performs a garbage collection sweep by copying every live record forward in log order and truncating the log by writing the new head. It achieves idempotency because liveness is positional: a record is dead only if a later `QDEL` covers its URL, a bulk survives if any of its chunks is live, and a tombstone survives while an older kept record still carries its URL. Consequently, compacting an already compacted log rewrites the same pages to the same places and generates the same merkle root, which is the fold of the live chunk hashes stored in the superblock.

