You must explicitly use the `boundary` keyword to force garbage collection at a specific point and call `tidy` to reclaim resources, as the runtime does not automatically clean up temporaries created before a frame boundary. Failing to do so causes memory to persist indefinitely, leading to resource exhaustion.

