The selection signals are derived by first calculating the running minimums (tMax) for each axis to determine the nearest boundary. The X selector (selX) is generated by comparing the X tMax value against the current X coordinate, while the Y selector (selY) is computed by multiplying this result by the negation of the X selector. Finally, the Z selector (selZ) is obtained by subtracting the Y selector from the negation of the X selector.

```sol
# selX = (tmxE == m1)
# selY = (tmxE == m1) * (1 - selX)
# selZ = (1 - selX) - selY

(sx1, sxr1) = Vec.dup (Vec.zipEq tmxE m1);
(nx1, nx2) = Vec.dup (Vec.axpb (0 - 1) 1 sx4);
(sy1, syr1) = Vec.dup (Vec.zipMul (Vec.zipEq tmyE m2) nx1);
(sz1, szr1) = Vec.dup (Vec.zipSub nx2 sy4);
```

