```fprisc
// Old approach: Each session polls individually (inefficient)
actor sessionReader {
    loop {
        poll(socket);
        process();
    }
}

// New approach: Single actor polls all sockets efficiently
actor main {
    poller = std/poller.fpr();
    loop {
        poller.poll();
        // Readers and acceptor sleep in mailboxes until notified
    }
}
```

The system now uses a single actor to poll all sockets via one `poll(2)` system call (implemented as `std/poller.fpr` over `Os.poll` and the runtime's `receiveNow`), allowing readers and the acceptor to sleep in their mailboxes instead of polling individually. This reduces the CPU cost of 1,000 idle sessions from half a core to 4% of one core.

