The `srvSend` function initiates the response transmission via `netWrite`, immediately closes the connection with `netClose`, and then discards the associated buffer by calling `bufDel` before proceeding to the next state. This sequence ensures that the connection is fully released and its resources cleaned up before the server continues processing.

```fprisc
srvSend mt cfg app sv cid resp quit =
  Sv model sess nsid ltt bufs = sv;
  _ = netWrite cid resp;
  _ = netClose cid;
  srvNext mt cfg app (Sv model sess nsid ltt (bufDel bufs cid)) quit.
```

The `srvSend` function handles a response by writing it to the network using `netWrite`, immediately closing the connection with `netClose`, and releasing the associated buffer via `bufDel` before passing control to `srvNext`. If the next request identifier is `1`, the server terminates the session by calling `srvBye`; otherwise, it loops back to `srvLoop` to continue processing.

```fpr
srvSend mt cfg app sv cid resp quit =
  Sv model sess nsid ltt bufs = sv;
  _ = netWrite cid resp;
  _ = netClose cid;
  srvNext mt cfg app (Sv model sess nsid ltt (bufDel bufs cid)) quit.

srvNext mt cfg app sv 1 = srvBye sv.
srvNext mt cfg app sv q = srvLoop mt cfg app sv.
```

