To calculate proportional dimensions, use the `propW` and `propH` functions with the font size `e` and text `t`, which divide the advance and line metrics by 1000. To enforce a width limit, the `textSize` function applies this calculation and then checks if the resulting width exceeds the character capacity defined by `ellipOf`; if it does, it caps the width to that capacity while retaining the original height. This logic ensures text fits within proportional constraints or falls back to fixed sizes if the font size is invalid.

```fprisc
textSize a n t =
  e = fsOf a;
  (w, h) = case e > 0 of
    True -> (propW t e, propH e)
  | False -> (textW n (scOf a), textH (scOf a));
  cap = ellipOf a;
