The files in the `machine/` directory constitute the machine layer, which defines the minimal set of functions the runtime requires to interact with the underlying hardware or host system. This layer is part of porting the language rather than an operating system, providing essential capabilities such as console I/O, power management, inter-processor interrupts, timing, context switching, and stack guarding. These functions are implemented separately for each target system, such as virtual machines, POSIX environments, or built-in targets.

