// Translucent instances are rendered second (blend, no depth write)
render translucent_instances;
```

Walker instances in the TERRA2 rendering pass utilize an alpha channel appended to the standard color triple, resulting in a four-component tuple (r, g, b, a). This allows for transparency effects where units fade out, such as smoke thinning, sparks dissolving, and destroyed units shrinking and fading over twenty seconds. The rendering pipeline draws opaque instances first, followed by translucent ones that are depth-tested but not depth-written, sorted from far to near to ensure correct visual blending.

