The ESP-IDF runtime in FP-RISC is an RTOS that owns the machine, boot, interrupts, heap, and both cores, yet lacks a process model, virtual memory, or file system unless explicitly requested. In contrast, the POSIX model treats the runtime as a process that borrows OS-supplied services like threads, virtual memory, signals, and a file system.

