j1 = fillR (Vec.new Unit) 1 100;
j2 = Vec.filter (fn p -> p.x > 90) j1;
j3 = Vec.map (fn p -> {p | y = p.y + 1}) j2;
(js, j4) = Vec.fold sumR 0 j3;
```

Chaining `Vec.map` operations results in a fused sequence of transformations, where the outer pair of maps fuses together before applying the subsequent function. When folding this chained result with a sum operation starting from 0, the expected total is the sum of the transformed values, which equals `r3 1 200` (representing 3 * 1 * 200).

```fprisc
