```

The "CLAIM-THEN-MASK" discipline prevents interrupt storms by ensuring that a level-triggered source, which keeps its line high until serviced, does not re-pend the interrupt immediately after the drain loop finishes processing it. When a source is claimed, the drain masks it; only after the actor completes its service and re-arms the source (via `Sys.irqAck`) does the gateway re-pend if the line is still high, guaranteeing exactly-once delivery per acknowledgment.
