The `port` function continuously loops, receiving messages from an actor and queuing them until it encounters a `PDrain` signal. Upon draining, it flushes the queued messages to a sender in reverse order, drops the received message, and clears the queue before resuming the loop. This mechanism ensures that queued roots persist across receives but are dropped after the drain reply's deep copy, guaranteeing that model updates occur transactionally at frame boundaries without interruption.

```fprisc
port me = portLoop me Nil
  where
    portLoop me q =
      m = receive me;
      case m of
        PDrain from -> portFlush me m from q
      | _ -> portLoop me (m :: q);
    portFlush me m from q =
      _ = send from (revK Nil q);
      _ = drop m;
      _ = portDropAll q;
      portLoop me Nil;
    portDropAll l = case l of Nil -> 0 | x :: r -> portDrop1 r x
      where portDrop1 r x = _ = drop x; portDropAll r.
```

