A QOS driver is defined as any software component that involves a first-order use of the QOS HAL API, meaning it directly calls QOS HAL functions. While everything above a driver is considered application or library code, a driver is also classified as library code but not an executable program by itself. Crucially, a QOS driver is a software component for a single device that forms a closed algebra, providing a well-formed set of operations that work consistently and predictably without redundant or conflicting actions.

```sol
// Incorrect usage: Application code directly calling HAL functions
// This violates the definition of a driver and breaks the closed algebra structure.
uart_start(); 
uart_write(0x00);

// Correct usage: A driver encapsulates HAL calls to form a closed algebra
// The driver provides the interface, while the application uses the driver.
uart_driver_start(); 
uart_driver_write(0x00);
```

