The previous 64-slot limit was reduced to 24 simultaneous watchers (IRQ IDs 1000–1023) because the former exceeded the IRQ controller's range, causing excess opens to fail explicitly rather than creating unusable watchers. Regarding `Os.watchClose`, it initiates shutdown without joining a worker on an actor's hart; it returns `False` to yield and retry, or `True` only when buffers are finished and the handle is released. Users must stop issuing `arm` or `take` calls before closing, finish the handshake, and never reuse the handle after `True` is returned.

