When a hart's backlog exceeds DONATE_HI, it deterministically donates its oldest entry (preserving the actor's stamp) into a machine-wide FIFO under a single lock, ensuring migrated actors retain their age and are served oldest-first without victim scanning. This process tightens admission bounds because donation never resets aging, and the worst-case time for an admission slot (T_slot) is defined by the sum of the compiler-emitted fuel quantum multiplied by the maximum segment size and hardware cost, the sum of C-entry bounds on the execution path, and scheduling overhead comprising ring draining, a backlog scan, and a constant-time steal lock hold.

```fpr
// Example: Actor with age > tau outranks un-aged actors; donation preserves stamp.
actor main {
    receive(m) -> {
        // Deterministic steal ensures oldest-stamped work is processed first.
        if (backlog > DONATE_HI) {
            donate_head(); // Preserves stamp, no age reset.
        }
        // Wait bound: tau * T_slot + A * T_slot.
        process(m);
    }
}
```

