When the requested size exceeds the remaining capacity, `realloc` triggers a memory move. It first calculates the available space, and if insufficient, allocates a new block, copies the data from the old block to the new one, frees the old block, and returns the address of the new block.
```fprisc
grow b v bytes =
  cap = Word.sub (Block.size b) (w (Block.sizeOf Unit));
  case i bytes <= i cap of
    True -> v
  | False -> move v bytes (i cap).
move v bytes cap =
  n = alloc bytes;
  _ = copyWords n v (cap / 8);
  _ = free v;
  n.
```

