The file `fprisc/sol/examples/bad_leak.sol` serves as a demonstration of a resource leak error in the FP-RISC Sol scripting language. It illustrates the critical necessity of explicitly closing file handles after operations to prevent data corruption or system instability. Although the code successfully writes data to a temporary file, it fails to invoke the close operation on the handle `h`, leaving the file descriptor open and unused.

