To compute the sum of a vector of numbers, you define a `plus` gate for addition and a `fill` gate to generate the vector, then use `Vec.fold` with `plus` and an initial zero value. The resulting sum must be identical regardless of whether the execution tier is interpreter, JIT, or GPU, as the checksum is invariant across tiers.

```sol
plus a b = a + b .

fill : Vector -> (i : Int | measure (lim - i)) -> (lim : Int) -> Vector .
fill v i lim | i > lim = v.
fill v i lim = fill (Vec.push (Num.sqrt (i * i)) v) (i + 1) lim.

> xs = fill (Vec.new Unit) 1 120000;
  ys = Vec.map poly xs;
  (s, ys2) = Vec.fold plus 0 ys;
  u = print "dispatch: checksum = {s}";
