To create a box background with an inset border, use the `boxBg` function. If the border color is defined, it calculates the border offset (`i`) and renders a rectangle inset by one pixel on all sides with the border color. If no border exists but a translucent background (`Bga`) is defined, it renders the background inset by the same amount. If neither is present, it returns the original color.

```fprisc
boxBg c a x y w h d =
  (has, col) = bgOf a;
  (hasA, colA) = bgaOf a;
  (hasB, colB) = bordOf a;
  i = case hasB of True -> 1 | False -> 0;
  r = roundOf a;
  ri = case r > 0 of True -> r - i | False -> 0;
  case has of
    True -> rrect c (x + i) (y + i) (w - 2 * i) (h - 2 * i) ri d (opaque col)
  | False -> case hasA of
      True -> rrect c (x + i) (y + i) (w - 2 * i) (h - 2 * i) ri d colA
    | False -> c.
```

