When the animation clock advances and the condition `done == 0` and `t2 >= durOf kind / 2` is true, the function calls `midpoint` to apply the rule, updates the time to `t2`, and sets the animation state to `An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 1`. If the animation type is less than 4, the snap value is increased by `auto * bi (kind < 4)`. If the condition is false, the state remains unchanged. Once the end condition `t2 >= durOf kind` is met, `finishAn` is called to clear the animation.

```fpr
m1 = case done == 0 and t2 >= durOf kind / 2 of
  True -> { (midpoint m kind s fz fc tz tc) | anim = An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 1, snap = m.snap + m.auto * bi (kind < 4) }
| False -> { m | anim = An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 done };
```

