The file `fprisc/std/live.fpr` defines the core logic for the live update mechanism in the QOS operating system, specifically handling the sequence of journaling events, persisting state changes, notifying writers, and managing session lifecycle. It ensures that updates are applied atomically by first journaling the event, then updating the model, persisting the new state, and finally broadcasting the version increment to all active writers before either settling the update or terminating the session.

```fprisc
advance : Int -> Ev m -> Rs -> O.Option Rs .
advance me ev st = case st of Rs cfg app model sessions nextSid db saved tickers version told ->
  _ = (if cfg.journal then journal app.codec db ev else Unit);
  (case app.update ev model of (model2, cmds) ->
      saved2 = persist me app.fields db model2 saved;
      quit = perform me sessions cmds;
      told2 = broadcast me (M.values sessions) (version + 1) told;
      (if quit then _ = settle app.fields db model2 saved2; _ = goodbye (M.values sessions); O.None
       else O.Some (startTickers me (Rs cfg app model2 sessions nextSid db saved2 tickers (version + 1) told2)))).
```

The `advance` function advances the simulation by first journaling the event if configured, then updating the application model to generate new commands, persisting the state, and finally notifying all active sessions of the state change. If the application decides to quit, it settles the state and terminates all sessions; otherwise, it restarts tickers with the updated version number.

```fpr
