The `load` function retrieves a page of entries from a store, either by directly accessing a page index for empty queries or by searching for matches when a query string is provided. It calculates the total number of pages required to display all results by dividing the count by the page size and rounding up. Finally, it adjusts the page index to the last page if the requested index exceeds the total available pages, ensuring the view displays valid data.

```sol
load store v =
  q = String.toLower v.q;
  (rows, n) = (if strlen q == 0 then Store.page (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store
               else Store.search (matches q) (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store);
  pages = (if n == 0 then 1 else (n + pageSize - 1) / pageSize);
  (if v.page >= pages and v.page > 0 then load store {v | page = pages - 1}
   else {rows = rows, count = n, total = (if strlen q == 0 then n else Store.count store), pages = pages, page = v.page}).
```

