The file `qos/programs/mods/liveview.fpr` implements the `/live/event` endpoint for the liveview module, which handles real-time event updates for clients identified by a unique session ID (sid). It processes incoming requests to either return a delta of changes since the client last polled or a full state snapshot, depending on whether the request contains the `__poll` marker. The logic first checks if the message is `__poll`; if so, it returns an empty delta indicating no new events. Otherwise, it retrieves the client's stored state, computes the difference (delta) between the previous and current state, and returns either the delta or the full state as JSON, ensuring clients only receive relevant updates.

```fpr
-- Example of handling a non-poll request to return a delta
srvEv2 mt cfg app sv cid sid msg arg | G.strEq msg "__poll" = srvReply mt cfg app sv cid sid 0
srvEv2 mt cfg app sv cid sid msg arg =
  App ini upd sbs vw = app;
  Sv model sess nsid ltt bufs = sv;
  (m2, cs) = upd cfg.env (EMsg msg arg) model;
  srvReply mt cfg app (Sv m2 sess nsid ltt bufs) cid sid (quitOf cs 0).
```

The `srvEvent` function is called to process an event request, requiring five arguments: an unsafe integer (`mt`), a configuration (`cfg`), an application (`app`), a server state (`sv`), a client ID (`cid`), and the request (`req`). Internally, it extracts the request body and calls `srvEv2`. When the extracted message equals the string "__poll", `srvEv2` triggers a polling response by calling `srvReply` with a quit code of 0, returning only the current state delta without a full snapshot. This behavior is defined within the `srvEv2` pattern matching logic: `srvEv2 mt cfg app sv cid sid msg arg | G.strEq msg "__poll" = srvReply mt cfg app sv cid sid 0.`

```sol
srvEvent mt cfg app sv cid req =
  body = bodyOf req;
  srvEv2 mt cfg app sv cid (cookieSid req) (jStr body "msg") (jStr body "arg");
```

