`buddy_realloc` is a mechanism for memory reallocation that handles in-place growth via buddy-absorb, in-place shrink, and copy fallback, while preserving coalescing after 20k randomized rounds. It was proven by the test script `qos/tests-host/buddy-check.sh`.

```sol
// Conceptual example of the mechanism's logic flow
if (needGrow) {
    absorbBuddy()
} else if (canShrink) {
