The file `tests/vecfuse2.fpr` serves as a benchmark to verify that the FP-RISC compiler successfully fuses a three-map chain into a single pass and optimizes the composition of `Vec.fold` with `Vec.map` into one operation that writes back and folds simultaneously. It validates that the compiler collapses the outer pair of maps in the first round and the composite over the inner map in the second round, ensuring that map writes remain program-visible through the returned vector during the fold process. The test confirms these optimizations by checking that the final sum matches a reference calculation and that memory usage remains low, specifically verifying the success of the chain-sum, chain-inplace, wfold-sum, wfold-writeback, and wfold-inplace transformations.

```fpr
main =
  v0 = Vec.range 1 1000;

  h0 = heapUsed Unit;
  v1 = Vec.map inc v0;
  v2 = Vec.map dbl v1;
  v3 = Vec.map mneg v2;
  h1 = heapUsed Unit;
  (s1, v4) = Vec.fold addA 0 v3;
