```

The `resolveAttack` function handles overwatch and ambush by chaining `intercept` and `ambush` calls. It checks if the attacker is still alive after these effects; if dead, it logs a failure message. If alive, it calculates damage based on whether the target is a headquarters or a unit, applying the appropriate modifier. The `spend` function is used to mark the attacker as having expended its action.

```sol
resolveAttack m s c tz tc =
  m1 = intercept m s c tc;
  m2 = ambush m1 s c tz tc;
  a = slotOf (sideOf m2 s) 1 c;
  case alive a of
    False -> note m2 "the attacker fell before striking"
  | True -> landBlow (spend m2 s 1 c) s c tz tc a.atk.
landBlow m s c 3 tc dmg = damageHq m (1 - s) dmg.
landBlow m s c tz tc dmg = damageUnit m (1 - s) tz tc dmg.
spend m s z c =
  p = sideOf m s;
  u = slotOf p z c;
  setSide m s (setSlot p z c { u | ready = 0, chg = 0 }).
```

