The `scanLocals` function iterates over all elements with an `x-data` attribute, splits the attribute value by semicolons, and parses key-value pairs separated by an equals sign. It populates a `locals` object only if the variable name is not already present, converting the value to a string.

```sol
def scanLocals(root) -> locals:
  locals = Object.create(null)
  root.querySelectorAll('[x-data]').forEach(el -> {
    attr := el.getAttribute('x-data')
    attr.split(';').forEach(pair -> {
      if pair is empty then return
      eq := pair.indexOf('=')
      name := pair.slice(0, eq)
      if name not in locals then
        locals[name] := pair.slice(eq + 1)
    })
  })
  return locals
```

The `scanLocals` function initializes the client-side state object by parsing the `x-data` attribute from all elements in the DOM that contain it. It iterates through the selected elements, splits the attribute value by semicolons to separate key-value pairs, and stores the parsed values in the `locals` object. This allows the client to track state that was declared in the server's template but is managed locally on the client side.

```fpr
function scanLocals() {
  root.querySelectorAll('[x-data]').forEach(function (el) {
    el.getAttribute('x-data').split(';').forEach(function (pair) {
      if (!pair) return;
      var eq = pair.indexOf('='), n = pair.slice(0, eq);
      if (!(n in locals)) locals[n] = pair.slice(eq + 1);
    });
  });
}
```

