The file `fprisc/sol/examples/plotdemo.sol` serves as a demonstration of the SVG/SMIL plotting backend by generating self-contained text files that browsers render into charts and animations. It implements pure arithmetic simulations using Euler-Cromer integrators to model a damped spring, gradient descent on a paraboloid, and two-body orbits, with the wave simulation utilizing a rational bump function instead of trigonometry. Running the script with `fpr sol plotdemo.sol` produces output files such as `plot-spring.svg`, `plot-descent.svg`, and animated SVGs for the wave and orbit simulations.

```sol
# Example of the damped spring simulation found in plotdemo.sol
spring k t x v | k <= 0 = ([], []).
spring k t x v =
  v2 = v + (0 - 4) * x * 0.05 - 0.3 * v * 0.05;
  x2 = x + v2 * 0.05;
  (pxs, pvs) = spring (k - 1) (t + 0.05) x2 v2;
  ((t, x) :: pxs, (t, v) :: pvs).
```

The `spring` function recursively simulates a damped spring system using an Euler-Cromer integrator based on the differential equation $x'' = -4x - 0.3v$. The integer parameter `k` acts as a step counter that terminates the recursion when it reaches zero, while the function accumulates time-series data for position and velocity. It calculates the next velocity by applying a damping factor of 0.3 and a restoring force derived from the position, then updates the position using the new velocity before recursing with the incremented time step.

```sol
spring k t x v | k <= 0 = ([], []).
spring k t x v =
  v2 = v + (0 - 4) * x * 0.05 - 0.3 * v * 0.05;
  x2 = x + v2 * 0.05;
  (pxs, pvs) = spring (k - 1) (t + 0.05) x2 v2;
  ((t, x) :: pxs, (t, v) :: pvs).
```

The function `clash` returns a new game state where both units are removed from the opposing sets, the environment variable is increased by 2 to reflect the two casualties, and logs are appended detailing the clash and the resulting casualties. Specifically, it calculates the resulting health for both units, determines that two kills occurred, updates the environment using `capEnv` with an increment of 2, and appends the casualty log.

```sol
clash k u d g =
  u2 = {u | hp = u.hp - max0 (d.atk - u.sh), used = 1};
  d2 = {d | hp = d.hp - max0 (u.atk - d.sh)};
  kills = boolInt (u2.hp <= 0) + boolInt (d2.hp <= 0);
