When calling a HAL function, you must treat it as a black box that consumes a fixed amount of fuel defined by your WCET model; the callee does not decrement fuel. Arguments passed to the HAL are borrowed, meaning the callee must increment the reference count (promote) any pointers it stores or returns. You must ensure the HAL function is bounded or yields via the actor machinery rather than spinning, as blocking or spinning outside the fuel budget holds the hart.

```fprisc
