The function `bWrap` constructs a bordered list of lists by wrapping an inner list with top and bottom borders and side columns. It takes a column identifier, a width, and an inner list, then creates a top border row, a bottom border row, and fills the sides with vertical border cells. The result is a list of lists where the first and last elements are border rows, and the middle elements have the specified column as their first and last elements.

```fprisc
borderW col child sz =
  (w, h) = sz;
  bWrap col w (child (w - 2, h - 2)).
bWrap col w inner =
  hb = mkCell 45 col 0;
  vb = mkCell 124 col 0;
  cn = mkCell 43 col 0;
  bar = cn :: append (repCell hb (w - 2)) (cn :: Nil);
  append (bar :: bMid vb inner) (bar :: Nil).
```

