The function `paintLocals` returns nothing (undefined) and performs side effects by updating the DOM. It iterates through all elements with `data-text` attributes to set their text content based on local variables, toggles visibility for elements with `data-show` attributes by comparing local values against specified strings or truthiness, and toggles the `is-on` CSS class on elements with `data-on` attributes if their corresponding local variable matches the specified value.

```fprisc
function paintLocals() \{
    root.querySelectorAll('[data-text]').forEach(function (el) \{
      el.textContent = locals[el.getAttribute('data-text')] ?? '';
    });
    root.querySelectorAll('[data-show]').forEach(function (el) \{
      var spec = el.getAttribute('data-show').split(':');
      var v = locals[spec[0]];
      var on = spec.length > 1 ? String(v) === spec[1]
                               : (v && v !== '0' && v !== 'false');
      el.style.display = on ? '' : 'none';
    });
    root.querySelectorAll('[data-on]').forEach(function (el) \{
      var spec = el.getAttribute('data-on').split(':');
      el.classList.toggle('is-on', String(locals[spec[0]]) === spec[1]);
    });
  }
```

Fuel is a resource consumed by each actor as it executes to enforce cooperative yielding. When an actor's fuel runs out, it must voluntarily yield control back to the scheduler to prevent starvation and manage resource usage.

```fprisc
actor main() {
    let fuel = 10;
    while (fuel > 0) {
        // Perform work
        fuel = fuel - 1;
        if (fuel == 0) {
            // Yield control when fuel is exhausted
            yield();
        }
    }
}
```

The FP-RISC actor model uses fuel for cooperative yielding, where each actor consumes fuel during execution and must yield control back to the scheduler when it runs out. This contrasts with garbage collection, which is absent in FP-RISC; instead, memory management relies on lambda lifting, linear types, and reference counting (RC) to handle immutable data structures and first-class functions without a GC.

```fprisc
let actor = spawn fun () ->
  let fuel = 10 in
  fuel > 0 do {
    std.println "Running";
    fuel := fuel - 1;
    actor;
  };
```

