EXTERN functions represent the driver VM calling Sol code, where arguments are spilled to frame slots and the fuel cell pointer is parked in a callee-saved register for the entire call tree. INTERNAL functions represent compiled Sol variants where arguments reside as the top `n` stack words and the result is returned directly onto the stack.

```sol
; EXTERN example: called by the VM driver
@extern_add (fuel_ptr: i64, a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 {
  push fuel_ptr
  push a
  push b
  Bin AddI
  Ret
}

; INTERNAL example: compiled Sol variant
@internal_add (a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 {
  push a
  push b
  Bin AddI
  Ret
}
```

