In the FP-RISC heap allocator, every block consists of a 64-byte header followed by a 16-byte meta pair containing capacity and reference count, with the payload starting at an offset of 80 bytes. To access the meta pair, one must first locate the block's base address, then add the offset of 64 bytes to reach the meta pair. The following Sol function illustrates retrieving the capacity from this meta pair:

```sol
fn get_capacity(block: Addr) -> Int {
    let meta_addr = block + 64
    let meta = read_block(meta_addr)
    meta.capacity
}
```

