u2 = appendNow @/tmp/rt-live.log "progress: step 2\n";
s = readNow @/tmp/rt-live.log;
print "readNow saw {String.len s} bytes already on disk".
```

In Sol, `writePath` buffers data until a transactional commit, meaning the text is not yet on disk when printed, whereas `appendNow` and `readNow` operations force immediate I/O to and from the disk. To observe real-time subprocess output, `shNow` executes a command and streams its result directly to the script's output without buffering.

```sol
