Sys.sleepUs is a parked sleep where the actor is placed on the hart's sleeper list with a deadline; it blocks until the hart-loop wakes it or an early wake message arrives, at which point it re-parks. Historically, this sleep affected the hart's thread, causing all actors sharing that hart to wait out the duration, including the memory actor and every system allocation. To prevent corruption, an actor currently in the run queue (admitted but not popped) is never added to the backlog again. This rule ensures that if a waker's message arrives late and flips the actor to READY, the actor runs and parks again before the stale push arrives, avoiding a self-pointing loop in the run queue.

```sol
