```fprisc
// Example: A heap operation using the migrated FP-RISC layout
let heap_ptr = make_heap();
let block = heap_ptr;
// The layout expands at parse time, costing nothing at runtime
let data = read_block(block);
```

Use the existing migration tool with the `--lib --export` flags to generate the necessary exports. Replace the original `heap.c` with the ported `heap.fpr` file, ensuring the environment variable `HEAP=fpr` is set to enable the new typed memory layout. This allows the same C symbols to be used while leveraging the nominal pointer types that expand at parse time without runtime cost.

