The runtime will fail to deliver the interrupt to any actor because the mechanism relies on the host thread raising an interrupt specifically for a bound actor. In the FP-RISC architecture, the job broker and posix watcher share this design where `hal_irq_raise` is invoked by a host thread to trigger a specific bound actor. If the target actor is not bound, the interrupt signal is ignored or lost, preventing the actor from executing its logic.

