  case n == 0 of
    True -> boot1 me ld
  | False -> boot2 me ld n.
```

The QOS system preserves state across reboots by recording the "attach chain" of live applications as persistent records on the disk's log during the initial boot, which the Loader reassembles automatically upon the next boot without requiring recompilation or explicit loading commands. The boot log provides evidence through the `sysdisk` test, which demonstrates that a hot swap performed in the first boot (resulting in `sysed2` being live) survives a reboot; the second boot logs a successful replay where the system immediately recognizes the persisted live set and executes the swapped application (`[Three]`) without any manual intervention.

