Work stealing tightens the wait time bound because donated actors preserve their original stamp and are served oldest-first from the machine-wide FIFO, preventing migration from resetting aging. Consequently, an actor's wait time is strictly bounded by its age multiplied by the worst-case slot time plus the number of resident actors on its hart multiplied by the slot time, as no newer actors can be admitted ahead of it once its age exceeds the threshold tau.

```fpr
