// The scheduler will pick this actor before any un-aged actors
// and donate it to the machine-wide FIFO if the backlog exceeds DONATE_HI
```

Deterministic work stealing preserves the actor's age (stamp) during migration, ensuring that donated actors remain in the machine-wide FIFO and are served oldest-first without resetting their age. Consequently, migration tightens wait bounds rather than increasing them. The worst-case wait time for an actor is bounded by the sum of its age times the worst-case slot time and the total number of resident actors times the slot time: Wait(a) <= tau * T_slot + A * T_slot. The admission slot time T_slot is determined by the fuel quantum, segment maximum, hardware cost, and specific code path bounds.

```fpr
