The `std/store` implementation compacts one small shard at a time, rewriting only the file of a specific shard when superseded lines outnumber live ones. Any data or structures built inside a shard actor that must survive a tidy operation must be stored within the tidied value itself; failing to keep them inside the state causes the path to dangle after the first reset.

