  Proc.spec (
    ["tar", "-czf", "archive.tar.gz", "."]
  )
);
```

No, a `Proc.afterCommit` command cannot run in an abandoned transaction attempt. Because deferred commands run in order after the filesystem commit and are recoverable from the redo journal, they require at-least-once execution semantics, meaning the command must tolerate repetition.

