The image size varies because the `buddy_reserve_range` fix alters how memory pages are allocated for plugin windows. Without the fix, a 1 GiB plugin window with 16,384 per-unit writes consumes 64 MiB of RAM (one 4 KiB page per write), resulting in a smaller total image footprint compared to systems or configurations where this optimization is applied.

