The fold will process stale or uninitialized values because the writes from the map have not yet been committed to the heap. This causes the fold to see incorrect data, leading to a wrong result. For example, if `Vec.map` writes are not landed, `Vec.fold` on the returned vector will not see the doubled elements, causing the final sum to be incorrect:
