The `items` function in `fprisc/std/json.fpr` parses a JSON array by recursively consuming values separated by commas until it encounters a closing bracket. It handles whitespace, validates the structure, and returns a `Sequence` containing the reversed list of values along with the index of the next character. Below is the Sol implementation of this logic:

```sol
fun items(s: String, i: Int, acc: List Value) -> Result (Value, Int) (Int, String) {
    if charAtOr(s, i) == ']' {
        if acc == Nil {
            return Ok(Sequence(Nil), i + 1)
        } else {
            return Err(i, "expected a value after ','")
        }
    }
    case value(s, i) {
        Err(e) -> return Err(e)
        Ok(v, next) -> return items(s, skip(s, next), v :: acc)
    }
}
```

