Fuel acts as a cooperative execution quantum that ensures every unbounded control path passes a safepoint. It is consumed specifically at the `exit` instruction of a function, which is the only point where a function can terminate without explicitly returning a value to the caller. This mechanism prevents infinite loops and allows the runtime to interrupt execution for safety checks or context switches.

```fprisc
