The `live.fpr` file defines the core state transition logic for the QOS operating system's event-driven execution model. It orchestrates the sequence where an event is first journaled, its effects are computed by the application, and the resulting state changes are persisted and broadcast to all active sessions before the system settles or terminates. This ensures that updates are visible to all writers in a consistent order.

```fprisc
advance me ev st = case st of Rs cfg app model sessions nextSid db saved tickers version told ->
  _ = (if cfg.journal then journal app.codec db ev else Unit);
  (case app.update ev model of (model2, cmds) ->
      saved2 = persist me app.fields db model2 saved;
      quit = perform me sessions cmds;
      told2 = broadcast me (M.values sessions) (version + 1) told;
      (if quit then _ = settle app.fields db model2 saved2; _ = goodbye (M.values sessions); O.None
       else O.Some (startTickers me (Rs cfg app model2 sessions nextSid db saved2 tickers (version + 1) told2)))).
```

The `advance` function first journals the event if configured, then updates the model and persists changes before notifying all active sessions of the new version. If the application quits, it settles the state and sends a stop signal to all writers; otherwise, it starts tickers and broadcasts the incremented version number to every writer that hasn't been notified yet.

```fprisc
advance me ev st = case st of
  Rs cfg app model sessions nextSid db saved tickers version told ->
    if cfg.journal then journal app.codec db ev else Unit;
    (model2, cmds) = app.update ev model;
    saved2 = persist me app.fields db model2 saved;
    quit = perform me sessions cmds;
    told2 = broadcast me (M.values sessions) (version + 1) told;
    if quit then
      settle app.fields db model2 saved2;
      goodbye (M.values sessions)
    else
      startTickers me (Rs cfg app model2 sessions nextSid db saved2 tickers (version + 1) told2);
    O.Some (result)
```

