This design isolates each peer's state, buffer, and statistics to its own actor, ensuring that a slow or hostile peer stalls only that specific actor without affecting the entire system. Sessions scale linearly with available memory rather than a central table, allowing the system to handle hundreds of concurrent connections efficiently. Each connection actor independently parses frames, sends events to the central register, and pushes its own delta, while the register acts as the single writer that broadcasts the updated model to all sessions.

