The `epoch` function performs a single pass over the dataset to compute gradients for the weight vectors and bias, applies L2 regularization, and updates the parameters using gradient descent. It iterates through the data using `Vec.fold` to accumulate sums of errors (`s1`, `s2`, `s3`) for each parameter, calculates the new weights by subtracting the learning rate times the average gradient plus the regularization term, and returns the updated parameters along with the final error sum.

```sol
epoch n lr w1 w2 b v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (hW1 w1 w2 b) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (hW2 w1 w2 b) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (hB w1 w2 b) 0 v2;
  w1n = w1 - lr * (s1 / n + lam * w1);
  w2n = w2 - lr * (s2 / n + lam * w2);
  (w1n, w2n, b - lr * (s3 / n), v3).
```

