The file `qos/programs/mods/uart.fpr` defines functional modules for initializing and configuring the UART (Universal Asynchronous Receiver-Transmitter) device within the QOS operating system. It implements two primary operations: `doOpen`, which claims device ownership and initializes the hardware registers to an 8N1 baud rate with interrupts disabled, and `doParams`, which allows the owner to modify the divisor latch to adjust the baud rate.

```fpr
doOpen me st from =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  case owner == 0 of
    False -> reply me from (UErr "uart is claimed") st
  | True -> doOpen2 me st from;

doOpen2 me st from =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  d2 = device "uart";
  _ = write (reg8 d2 3) 3;
  _ = write (reg8 d2 1) 0;
  reply me from UOk (St d2 from cap txq rxs sub fl 0);
```

The `doParams` function verifies ownership before configuring the UART divisor latch. It sets the divisor latch access bit (DLAB) to 1, writes the low and high bytes of the divisor value, and finally resets DLAB to 0 to restore the 8N1 mode.

```sol
doParams2 me st from d =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 131;
  _ = write (reg8 dev 0) (band d 255);
  _ = write (reg8 dev 1) (BITSHIFTR d 8);
  _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 3;
  reply me from UOk st.
```

