let chunks = Disk.qa.findChunks(fileId);
let fileData = Disk.qa.fold(chunks);
```

The data partition is append-only and bounded, functioning as a recursive chunk-based system where files are constructed by folding chunks identified by a URL-to-ID mapping. In contrast, the metadata partition is designed for modification and manages the logical structure of the storage, specifically tracking the HEAD pointer to the latest log entry and flags indicating write or commit status. While data relies on Merkle trees for integrity during compaction, metadata ensures the system can correctly locate and merge chunks for garbage collection.

```sol
