  u1 = mkdirp "{root}/test";
  u2 = writePath "{root}/README.md" "# {base.baseName root}\n\ngenerated by sol\n";
  u3 = writePath "{root}/src/main.sol" "> print \"hello from {base.baseName root}\".\n";
  u4 = writePath "{root}/test/basic.sol" "> print \"test stub\".\n";
  print "scaffolded {root} (4 files, 2 dirs) — atomic".
```

Each operation `u0` through `u4` returns a unit value (`u`) representing a deferred, atomic action that has been queued for execution. The final outcome is that the script prints the message "scaffolded {root} (4 files, 2 dirs) — atomic" only after all queued mutations (creating directories and writing files) have been successfully applied to the filesystem. This ensures the operation is either fully successful or fully failed, leaving no half-done state.

