The `buddy_realloc` mechanism manages memory through in-place growth via buddy absorption, in-place shrinkage, and a copy fallback after coalescing, verified by randomized rounds. In contrast, the contiguous `Vec` on `realloc` (Phase 2) simplifies the strategy to a single contiguous allocation, removing the complexity of buddy system coalescing and fallback copying.

```sol
