The POSIX core is designed to run on harts utilizing pthreads, with synchronization managed via park and wake on condition variables. This approach leverages the standard POSIX subset available on both host types to provide a consistent foundation for the clock, streams, sockets, and the watcher.

```sol
// Example of using the condition variable mechanism in the POSIX core
import std/io;
import std/sync;

actor watchdog {
    var cond: ConditionVariable;
    var running: Bool = true;

    start() {
        cond.init();
        while (running) {
            park(cond); // Blocks until signaled
        }
    }
}
```

