In native kernels, integer division by zero does not cause a panic within the code itself. Instead, the kernel explicitly poisons the fuel cell (setting it to -2^62) and returns 0. Upon returning to the VM, this poisoned fuel state triggers a panic with the message "SOL PANIC: division by zero".

Example:
```sol
# Native kernel
fn div_zero(fuel*, in*, n, out*) {
    let x = in[0];
    if (x == 0) {
        fuelPoison();
        out[0] = 0;
    } else {
        out[0] = in[0] / in[1];
    }
}
```

