#qos-portable
#include <qos_hal.h>

int main() {
    qos_hal_t hal;
    hal.init();
    // Access QOS services directly
    return 0;
}
```

The `posix` system treats the host operating system as the board, resulting in an ordinary executable that relies on standard OS services like files, sockets, and processes without needing any QOS runtime. In contrast, the `qos-portable` system produces a QOS app image that carries its own copy of the runtime and interacts exclusively with QOS's HAL and services, making the underlying host OS an implementation detail.

```sol
// Example: A program targeting POSIX (standard executable)
--system=posix
