An implementation of L alone constitutes only a language implementation. A claim of platform conformance to (L_n, S_n) additionally requires the whole mandatory Base contract, which includes the minimal specified boundary to the environment for effects like reading and writing. A program restricted to the L and Base pair is considered portable subject to its declared environmental capabilities and resource needs, acknowledging that different machines may have different permitted external inputs, timing, and failures.

