The `reconcile` function throws an `Error` with the message "duplicate view key: <key>" if it encounters a node that already exists in the keyed map or if a new node with the same key is added to the `wanted` list while iterating. This prevents the system from overwriting the mapping for a specific view key, ensuring unique identification of view elements.

```fprisc
function reconcile(parent, wanted) {
    var keyed = new Map();
    Array.from(parent.childNodes).forEach(function (n) {
      var key = keyOf(n);
      if (key !== null) {
