The `leadSlack` function calculates the available space by subtracting the total width of widgets and gaps from the container width minus padding, then divides the result by two if no widgets are growing. If widgets are growing, it returns zero. The calculation involves summing the widths and gaps of the children, comparing the count to determine gaps, and checking if any child has a growth capability.

```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

