The file `tools/build.sol` serves as the driver host for the FP-RISC toolchain, acting as a `make` replacement to orchestrate the build process without requiring external build systems. It utilizes Sol scripting to manage the compilation of the C runtime sources (core + posix) and the linking of the final static executable, ensuring the output remains isolated and reproducible. For example, it can be used to compile the runtime and link the application as shown below:

