The file `fprisc/sol/lib/logic.sol` defines core functional programming primitives for the FP-RISC Sol language, specifically implementing state management via a trail-based backtracking system and unification logic. It provides `trailPush` and `bind` to record bindings on a computation trail, enabling `undoTo` to backtrack and reset the heap and trail to previous states. Additionally, it includes `deref` for accessing cell values and `unify` to check for term equality, supporting the language's declarative nature.

```sol
bind a t v m = trailPush a (setCell a t v m);
unify a b m =
  (m1, a2, ta, va) = deref a m;
  (m2, b2, tb, vb) = deref b m1;
  case a2 == b2 of
    True -> (m2, True)
  | False -> unify2 a2 ta va b2 tb vb m2.
```

