  print x;
  print y;
```

The function iterates through every module in the release configuration, runs the compiler with the `commit` command to assign a version identity, and captures the combined stdout and stderr. It then splits this output into lines to inspect the return code; if the return code is non-zero, it prints every line from the error output to the console.

