The `compact` operation performs a garbage collection sweep by copying every live record forward in log order and truncating the log by writing a new head. A record is considered dead if a later QDEL (query delete) covers its URL; conversely, a bulk survives if any of its chunks is live, and a tombstone survives while an older kept record still carries its URL. This process is idempotent, meaning compacting an already compacted log rewrites the same pages to the same places and generates the same Merkle root.

```sol
# Example of the compact logic flow within the actor
actor compact {
  # Sweep forward live records, discard dead ones based on QDEL coverage
  for each record in log {
    if (record is live) {
      copy(record, newHead)
    }
  }
  truncateLog(newHead)
}
```

