While adding a span field to every constructor offers the best precision for diagnostics, it is avoided because it would force the compiler to touch every pattern match across all passes simultaneously. Instead, statement granularity is achieved via a wrapper that covers most of the value for a fraction of the computational churn, with the option to widen the span later if necessary. This approach is specifically designed to support LSP diagnostics providers by providing a `Name -> (file, line)` anchor map that can be checked efficiently without the overhead of full span tracking on every construct.

