The `part` function takes a column set, a list of values, and a threshold `t`, and splits the values into two lists: those less than or equal to `t` go into `al` (ascending), and those greater than `t` go into `ar` (ascending). It processes the input list recursively, retrieving the next value and its binning information from the column set to determine the split.

```fprisc
part cs Nil t al ar = (al, ar, cs);
part cs (i :: rest) t al ar =
