Previously, every actor allocating anything consumed a full 256 KiB slab, causing 1000 small actors to waste 508 MiB before working. This is now fixed so slabs start small and double in size until reaching 196 MiB. Additionally, the runtime object cache now treats an object as stale if any HEADER is newer than the object's own `.c` file, whereas it previously only compared objects against their own `.c` files, which could lead to crashes when structs in `fpr.h` changed.

```sol
