    // Object is stale and will be reloaded
    stale = true
}
```

A pool's slabs start small and double in size. The first slab is a single buddy block, and each subsequent slab is twice the size of the previous one, growing up to FPR_SLAB_SZ (196 MiB). This prevents actors from immediately consuming excessive memory; for instance, a thousand small session actors now only consume 508 MiB of arena before performing any work, whereas the previous approach would have required a whole FPR_SLAB_SZ (256 KiB) per actor.

```sol
// Example of slab growth logic concept
slab_size = 1 * FPR_BUDDY_BLOCK_SIZE
while (slab_size < FPR_SLAB_SZ) {
    slab_size = slab_size * 2
    allocate_slab(slab_size)
}
```

