A program can achieve this by first sending a `Frame` request to a spawned worker via `send`, then receiving the updated `Frame` message from the worker using `receiveFrom`. Once the new coordinates and state are extracted, the program calls itself recursively with the updated values to continue the loop. This pattern is demonstrated in the `run` function which sends a request, drops the sent message, receives the response, and invokes `nextFrame` to iterate.

```sol
run me worker x z keys buttons yaw pitch =
  request = Frame x z keys buttons yaw pitch;
  _ = send worker request;
  _ = drop request;
  message = receiveFrom me worker;
  Frame nextX nextZ nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch = message;
  _ = drop message;
