When the `session` actor accepts a request via `WS.accept`, it spawns a new writer actor using `A.spawnWith` to handle the protocol logic. It then asks itself for a `Join` result to ensure the writer is ready before proceeding. If the request succeeds, the actor extracts the session ID (`n`) from the `Welcome` message returned by the `Join` operation; if the ID is 0, no session tracking occurs.

```fprisc
session reg poller app conn req = case WS.accept req of
    Err why -> _ = ST.write (H.renderResponse (H.text 400 "{why}\n")) conn; Unit
  | Ok head ->
      _ = ST.write head conn;
      me = myself 0;
      writer = A.spawnWith (A.Dynamic 64) (fn self -> writerStart (protocolOf req.query) reg app conn self);
      r = A.askSure me reg (Join writer);
      sid = (case r of Welcome n _ -> n | _ -> 0);
      _ = drop r;
      (if sid == 0 then Unit else reading reg app.codec writer sid (ST.readerOn poller conn) conn A.tidySmall).
```

