```sol
moveEnemies m Nil dist flee acc = { m | ens = revEn acc Nil };
moveEnemies m (e :: r) dist flee acc =
  (m1, e2) = moveOne m e dist flee;
  moveEnemies m1 r dist flee (e2 :: acc);
```

The `load` function first converts the query string to lowercase and determines whether to retrieve a full page or a searched subset by checking the query length. If the query is empty, it fetches the page directly from the store; otherwise, it searches for matching entries and calculates the number of resulting pages using ceiling division. Finally, it adjusts the returned page index to ensure it stays within valid bounds, defaulting to the last page if the requested index exceeds the total count, and returns the updated entry with the retrieved rows, count, and total.

```fprisc
load store v =
  q = String.toLower v.q;
  (rows, n) = (if strlen q == 0 then Store.page (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store
               else Store.search (matches q) (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store);
  pages = (if n == 0 then 1 else (n + pageSize - 1) / pageSize);
  (if v.page >= pages and v.page > 0 then load store {v | page = pages - 1}
   else {rows = rows, count = n, total = (if strlen q == 0 then n else Store.count store), pages = pages, page = v.page}).
```

When the search query `q` is non-empty and yields zero matches (`n == 0`), the function calculates `pages` as 1. If the requested page index `v.page` is greater than or equal to this calculated page count (which is 1) and greater than 0, it recursively loads the previous page (`v.page - 1`) to display the last available content rather than an empty state. If `v.page` is 0 or less than the calculated page count, it returns the current page with zero rows and a total count of 0.

```fpr
load store v =
  q = String.toLower v.q;
  (rows, n) = (if strlen q == 0 then Store.page (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store
               else Store.search (matches q) (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store);
  pages = (if n == 0 then 1 else (n + pageSize - 1) / pageSize);
  (if v.page >= pages and v.page > 0 then load store {v | page = pages - 1}
   else {rows = rows, count = n, total = (if strlen q == 0 then n else Store.count store), pages = pages, page = v.page}).
```

