Standard function calls do not act as hardware memory barriers, so they fail to enforce the necessary ordering between memory and I/O domains. To ensure correct synchronization, the appropriate `Mem.fence` instruction must be used explicitly, as it corresponds to the hardware instruction `fence iorw, iorw`.

```sol
// Incorrect: Call alone does not provide memory/I/O ordering
