_ = Rc.release xs;
_ = print ys;
Rc.release ys.

You must not pass raw floats, ADTs containing raw floats, actors, vectors, mutable runtime objects, or function closures to the explicit reclamation API because floats carry untagged bits that cannot be distinguished from references during generic traversal, and cycles are unsupported. Additionally, borrowed references must not be released, and user code must never use an object after its last release.
