The program will fail because the Base contract explicitly prohibits requiring Unix paths, descriptors, or processes merely because the reference host uses them. An implementation must provide a generic interface defining acquisition, permission, absence, failure, ordering, and resource lifetime; assuming specific OS artifacts violates the portability requirements of the contract.

