When an actor encounters a message that does not match any condition in its `receive` block, the execution flow is halted for that specific message. The actor will not process the message, and depending on the underlying policy, it may block waiting for the next message or drop the message entirely. For example, if an actor is defined as `receive { Fail -> drop }`, any incoming message that does not satisfy the conditions in the block will be dropped without further processing.

```sol
receive {
    if (msg.type == "data") {
        process(msg);
    }
    // Missing condition for "error" type
}
```

This block defines the boundary condition for when an SPSC buffer is full, allowing the actor to decide whether to block, drop messages, or use other strategies. For example, an actor might define a fail strategy to drop incoming messages when the queue is full:
