On multi-core systems, device interrupts are routed to auxiliary harts, while the prime hart (0) does not handle them unless it is the only core available. This is implemented by enabling the hart's M context and interrupt draining exclusively on the last live hart via the PLIC. For a single-core system, hart-0 acts as both the prime and auxiliary hart, allowing it to receive device interrupts directly.

