The `leadSlack` function calculates the available space along the layout axis (width for rows, height for columns) by subtracting the total used space (sum of children's widths or heights plus gaps) from the available dimension, then divides the result by two. If any children are permitted to grow (`countGrow` is greater than zero), the function returns zero. Otherwise, it returns half of the remaining slack.
```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

