The QOS system sanitizes login names by stripping HTML markup and control characters, enforcing a maximum length of 24 bytes, and decoding valid UTF-8 while rejecting surrogate pairs (which appear as "??" in the UI). If a name is empty, the login is refused silently.

```sol
// Example of name handling logic (conceptual FP-RISC/Sol representation)
// 1. Strip markup/control chars:
name = stripMarkup(inputName)

// 2. Decode UTF-8, drop control bytes, reject surrogates:
name = decodeUTF8(name)

// 3. Enforce 24-byte cap (keeps characters whole):
if length(name) > 24:
    name = truncate(name, 24)

// 4. Reject empty names:
if name is empty:
    return refusal
```

